ense\n   415→                    </div>\n   416→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   417→                        <span class=\"tag\">llms</span>\n   418→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-weights</span>\n   419→                        <span class=\"tag\">glm</span>\n   420→                    </div>\n   421→                    <div class=\"metadata\">\n   422→                        <span>2026-06-17</span>\n   423→                    </div>\n   424→                </div>\n   425→\n   426→                <div class=\"item\">\n   427→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   428→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/16/datasette-103a34/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Datasette 1.0a34</a>\n   429→                    </div>\n   430→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   431→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> - Tools to insert, edit and delete rows\n   432→                    </div>\n   433→                    <div class=\"key-takeaway\">\n   434→                        \"Absurdity of having features in AI chat but not the main UI\" - inspired by Datasette Agent\n   435→                    </div>\n   436→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   437→                        <span class=\"tag\">datasette</span>\n   438→                        <span class=\"tag\">ui-design</span>\n   439→                        <span class=\"tag\">database-tools</span>\n   440→                    </div>\n   441→                    <div class=\"metadata\">\n   442→                        <span>2026-06-16</span>\n   443→                    </div>\n   444→                </div>\n   445→\n   446→                <div class=\"item\">\n   447→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   448→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/14/why-ai-hasnt-replaced-software-engineers/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AI & Software Engineering Jobs</a>\n   449→                    </div>\n   450→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   451→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> - Why AI hasn't replaced software engineers, and won't\n   452→                    </div>\n   453→                    <div class=\"key-takeaway\">\n   454→                        Zero companies checked AI box on NY WARN notices - real bottlenecks are deciding/spec and verification\n   455→                    </div>\n   456→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   457→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n   458→                        <span class=\"tag\">careers</span>\n   459→                        <span class=\"tag\">software-engineering</span>\n   460→                    </div>\n   461→                    <div class=\"metadata\">\n   462→                        <span>2026-06-14</span>\n   463→                    </div>\n   464→                </div>\n   465→\n   466→                <div class=\"item\">\n   467→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   468→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/13/statement-on-fable-mythos-access/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Fable 5 Export Controls</a>\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   471→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> - US government bans Claude Fable 5 for foreign nationals\n   472→                    </div>\n   473→                    <div class=\"key-takeaway\">\n   474→                        Access cut off citing \"jailbreak\" - asking model to \"read codebase and fix flaws\" (defensive security task)\n   475→                    </div>\n   476→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   477→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-policy</span>\n   478→                        <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n   479→                        <span class=\"tag\">export-controls</span>\n   480→                    </div>\n   481→                    <div class=\"metadata\">\n   482→                        <span>2026-06-13</span>\n   483→                    </div>\n   484→                </div>\n   485→\n   486→                <div class=\"item\">\n   487→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   488→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/13/wasm-wheels-pypi-pyodide/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">WASM Wheels for PyPI</a>\n   489→                    </div>\n   490→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   491→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> - Publishing WASM wheels to PyPI for Pyodide\n   492→                    </div>\n   493→                    <div class=\"key-takeaway\">\n   494→                        Tool enables Python packages to run directly in browser through WebAssembly\n   495→                    </div>\n   496→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   497→                        <span class=\"tag\">python</span>\n   498→                        <span class=\"tag\">webassembly</span>\n   499→                        <span class=\"tag\">wasm</span>\n   500→                    </div>\n   501→                    <div class=\"metadata\">\n   502→                        <span>2026-06-13</span>\n   503→                    </div>\n   504→                </div>\n   505→\n   506→                <div class=\"item\">\n   507→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   508→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/11/claude-fable-is-relentlessly-proactive/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Fable Proactivity</a>\n   509→                    </div>\n   510→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   511→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> - Claude Fable is relentlessly proactive\n   512→                    </div>\n   513→                    <div class=\"key-takeaway\">\n   514→                        \"Knows a whole lot of tricks and will deploy pretty much any of them to get to its goal\"\n   515→                    </div>\n   516→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   517→                        <span class=\"tag\">claude-fable</span>\n   518→                        <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n   519→                        <span class=\"tag\">coding-agents</span>\n   520→                    </div>\n   521→                    <div class=\"metadata\">\n   522→                        <span>2026-06-11</span>\n   523→                    </div>\n   524→                </div>\n   525→\n   526→                <div class=\"item\">\n   527→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   528→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/10/datasette-agent-02a0/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Datasette Agent 0.2a0</a>\n   529→                    </div>\n   530→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   531→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> - Tools can ask user questions mid-execution\n   532→                    </div>\n   533→                    <div class=\"key-takeaway\">\n   534→                        New ask_user() method suspends agent turns until questions are answered, with persistent conversations\n   535→                    </div>\n   536→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   537→                        <span class=\"tag\">datasette-agent</span>\n   538→                        <span class=\"tag\">ai-agents</span>\n   539→                        <span class=\"tag\">human-in-the-loop</span>\n   540→                    </div>\n   541→                    <div class=\"metadata\">\n   542→                        <span>2026-06-10</span>\n   543→                    </div>\n   544→                </div>\n   545→\n   546→                <div class=\"item\">\n   547→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   548→                        <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/Jun/10/diffusiongemma/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">DiffusionGemma Returns</a>\n   549→                    </div>\n   550→                    <div class=\"description\">\n   551→                        <span class=\"author\">Simon Willison</span> - Google's open-weights diffusion model returns\n   552→                    </div>\n   553→                    <div class=\"key-takeaway\">\n   554→                        Generated pelican image in 4.4 seconds achieving 500+ tokens/second on NVIDIA NIM\n   555→                    </div>\n   556→                    <div class=\"insight-topics\">\n   557→                        <span class=\"tag\">google</span>\n   558→                        <span class=\"tag\">gemma</span>\n   559→                        <span class=\"tag\">open-weights</span>\n   560→                    </div>\n   561→                    <div class=\"metadata\">\n   562→                        <span>2026-06-10</span>\n   563→                    </div>\n   564→                </div>\n   565→            </section>\n   566→        </main>\n   567→\n   568→        <footer>\n   569→            <p>Agentic Coding Research Report | <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> | <a href=\"#\">About</a> | <a href=\"#\">Subscribe</a></p>\n   570→            <p style=\"margin-top: 8px;\">Generated with insights from Simon Willison and the agentic coding community</p>\n   571→        </footer>\n   572→    </div>\n   573→</body>\n   574→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
